  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_d2cdcf05dd4149bb9ea0a5fb0d1568d8",
      "statement": "BaseChatModel is an abstract protocol class that all chat model implementations inherit from. It is a Runnable that accepts LanguageModelInput (PromptValue, string, or sequence of messages) and produces AIMessage outputs. Subclasses must implement _generate (required) and optionally _llm_type, _stream, _agenerate, and _astream methods.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L284-L332",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cfd32376cbed1e686d0204121882ac2c99a34deac67b48da8ef025034c33a85a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_827f2a3f82984673bc9aedc818bcec64",
      "statement": "BaseChatModel provides synchronous invoke/stream and asynchronous ainvoke/astream methods that handle message conversion, callback lifecycle (on_chat_model_start, on_llm_new_token, on_llm_end, on_llm_error), rate limiting, and routing to streaming or non-streaming code paths based on model implementation and configuration.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L474-L523",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9530ef00f9f42bd871ffa6b861c523bf4bd6383b0525873a8ef722979812dfd3:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L726-L990",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:145b830db054fb6650ec383cec82317fa44c9cd6bd173f2c6ce94ecbbf300aec:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_dc67358634a74aeba7bff0a85313ecf8",
      "statement": "The _should_stream() method determines whether to route through streaming APIs based on: (1) whether _stream/_astream are implemented, (2) disable_streaming configuration, (3) explicit stream=True/False kwargs, (4) instance-level streaming attribute, or (5) attached _StreamingCallbackHandler. If streaming is unavailable or disabled, stream() falls back to invoke() and yields a single chunk.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L525-L585",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:45eff9fcf247512c468032e165dd24e8c1ffc75e9a5f52d2780e137cad20140f:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L726-L741",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cacbd449489fb9444e90e81dcf1ccc0e634841564f80ffa8520f3805bd9e4dd2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_88a3bc68c8c44f8d8e90f4e8f99af29d",
      "statement": "Subclasses implement streaming via _stream() (sync) or _astream() (async) methods that yield ChatGenerationChunk objects. These methods receive normalized messages, stop sequences, and a run_manager for per-token callbacks. The default _astream implementation runs _stream in an executor. If neither is overridden, the model is non-streaming.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L2255-L2311",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:731ced876db905c6d0950307f17a0523039ddf745c88e7c76ca4f706c988ac19:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b7e494bdfca8440db5198397500c6093",
      "statement": "ChatModelStream and AsyncChatModelStream are returned by stream_events(version='v3') and expose typed projections (.text, .reasoning, .tool_calls, .usage, .output) that accumulate protocol events as they arrive. Each projection can be iterated for deltas or awaited for the final value.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_model_stream.py#L1-L46",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:da766bf0c8862bfef9808624d302620cb3140e480dcd61508c3351300de0cc2c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4241369e9483403b9c2cea053dc229da",
      "statement": "_generate() is the required abstract method all BaseChatModel subclasses must implement. It receives normalized BaseMessage list, optional stop sequences, and a run_manager. It returns a ChatResult containing a list of ChatGeneration objects (each holding an AIMessage and generation metadata).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L2208-L2226",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7dc9ec20b0a88c54a871331ce5f6dadd49655125dca20d86e156c6f2d752e509:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8c5628590b924439b189efce4c20ac96",
      "statement": "_agenerate() is an optional override for native async support. The default implementation runs _generate in an executor via run_in_executor. Subclasses override to call native async provider APIs.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L2228-L2253",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fac4b6218fce15d131280a4526267491b6aa6a769235926ebb676cacf677a1cf:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_2c69747d436f4b7e87260f3b184a7875",
      "statement": "_generate_with_cache() and _agenerate_with_cache() wrap the core generation methods to transparently check and populate prompt caches via self.cache or get_llm_cache(). Cache hits replay v2 events if attached handlers support them, providing transparent caching with consistent callback behavior.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L1892-L2206",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8875e363badb600e00e7b80f354fca72b52ecd03e88a1c87cc770026fe10e7cc:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_824b46e4e601461a84a96f8f83ce7cbe",
      "statement": "Chat models emit structured callback events throughout execution: on_chat_model_start (with serialized config and batch size), on_llm_new_token per streamed token, on_llm_end with final LLMResult, on_llm_error with exception, and on_stream_event for v2/v3 protocol events. Callbacks are configured via RunnableConfig with callbacks, tags, metadata, run_name, and run_id fields.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L1668-L1676",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1768cb9dcdfcc21004690fd656a760bc1260a60eb701db318f4c526426bcd74b:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L773-L855",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:19a352f161e0454121917f747b7c73cde8e4ad68cb5844e6ac77c6b8aa425847:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4e7ce7ec11bc4a44b5bf0f404f70fa26",
      "statement": "with_structured_output() constrains model output to a specified schema (Pydantic class, TypedDict, dict, or OpenAI tool schema). It delegates to bind_tools([schema], tool_choice='any') and chains through output parsers (PydanticToolsParser or JsonOutputKeyToolsParser). If include_raw=True, output is wrapped in {raw, parsed, parsing_error}. Requires bind_tools() implementation.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L2385-L2565",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:673bc22e396265b7dbabfa67b802837132337352be622cd69c071cfc5dfd1c84:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_fde81caf70274472a5807c28253e2d75",
      "statement": "bind_tools() is an abstract method that subclasses override to bind a sequence of tool definitions to the model. It accepts tools (dict, type, callable, or BaseTool), tool_choice parameter, and returns a Runnable[LanguageModelInput, AIMessage] that includes tool definitions in API requests.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L2366-L2383",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a2c56a9bc7a84b7ed47b879ac55e9139606dc73bd2023a8ced246310d05fb38c:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_a5942a521cca487ca5e1ca8f328163c9",
      "statement": "The ModelProfile TypedDict (optional field on BaseChatModel) holds capability metadata: context_window (max_input_tokens), supported modalities (text/image/audio/video/pdf inputs and outputs), tool calling support, structured output support, reasoning capabilities, and temperature support. Profiles are auto-loaded via _resolve_model_profile() override in subclasses.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L378-L444",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:8cff3df6f9a49eb1b3a5ba8ab37f259d084d3c6082f7da23b16c453c1d93cd72:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/model_profile.py#L13-L150",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:497a9318b6379350b195e046e266ed2e8ccd7b0e2c69aaa337f7eab0811059ea:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_af3159f29b2e4a53b9538a954ef8b5eb",
      "statement": "BaseChatModel automatically loads model profiles via Pydantic validator _set_model_profile (mode='after'). Subclasses override _resolve_model_profile() to return model-specific profile data; the validator handles assignment and error suppression. Partner packages override _resolve_model_profile() to load profiles from their own profile registries.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L398-L444",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f18d0b7106bc8237b8ffc290264d8d484ab6310f067a2375e15326297a177520:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_82543184d89c479aa3d772502f81c185",
      "statement": "The disable_streaming field controls streaming behavior: False (default) enables streaming if available; True disables all streaming; 'tool_calling' disables streaming only when tools are passed. This allows gradual model replacement and workarounds for models with broken streaming.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L337-L353",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:51a6022ded251d8aee989262f4639c607e5697637e91e32e9b6adecdc3b77836:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c8ecef7a6bac40fda27f1a0fa349d075",
      "statement": "The output_version field (v0 or v1) controls AIMessage content format in stream() and invoke(). When output_version='v1', content is overwritten with standardized content_blocks format before streaming chunks and final generation. This allows consistent output shape across legacy and new code paths.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L355-L376",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:635a4b31855a4187743c7ababe83b7c78224ee57efa89c5d27dda7a74b5faf3c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L798-L810",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:17453abba43b78a6ebc60d0c77c65844c04edc5eaad2f8ccc01c73366e30dfa5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_43a30b4ed6ca4fc0aecb33ce2ff1bc07",
      "statement": "BaseChatModel accepts optional rate_limiter field (BaseRateLimiter). When present, rate limiter is acquired (blocking) before _stream or _astream is called. This allows centralized request rate limiting across all calls to a model instance.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L334-L335",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:0fc1547d1be910cddd9353c31d20d343a35782557cdf49eca01c3c412bcb3314:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L785-L786",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cf9be61ceadd3f7e68f7bd2e4d1cccd7602eadd3d5746d5d8380986d58f8cd4c:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L916-L917",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:48256efe060f855bb4cc3b04cf89ff00b05eee9ec177da4b89bb9cc0c601f842:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_9238f8d4394949909b8bdf20533210ae",
      "statement": "Stream and generate methods normalize messages via _normalize_messages() before passing to _stream/_generate. Each streamed chunk and final message receive a unique ID (derived from run_id) via message.id assignment for tracing. A final empty chunk with chunk_position='last' is emitted when streaming completes.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L789-L827",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ed945de6b40629a7372acc7b08a9bf7dce32fbadd5b2aaa7f0c7ab3354b6a9fd:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L922-L968",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:dc2eb57b0164229b93dad722773090979a244f7d8890a7b87859edaeb90d8fed:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ec235df6cf964921ac38bf132ea90a74",
      "statement": "Each generation accumulates response metadata in AIMessage.response_metadata via _gen_info_and_msg_metadata(), which merges generation_info and message.response_metadata. For single-generation results, llm_output is also merged. This ensures all provider-specific metadata is accessible to the caller.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L2705-L2720",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:965fbb380f052092c2ab3b975d319f11de6c7062904ff58b40935569e5165aa0:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L797-L797",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:5cbd5b8f86a102c25aac35f771f6330bef7ce8d346a1a659d16f68807b8f42c8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cc5fae439d664a6a8f8097b04d84aa96",
      "statement": "_identifying_params (optional property) returns a dict of model configuration for tracing and cache key generation (e.g., {model: 'gpt-4', temperature: 0.7}). The _get_llm_string() method uses this to generate unique cache keys. Subclasses override to expose relevant configuration.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L1578-L1590",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:db996df4a774482474945b91b56b5c878e43df72cc2fbf7c176428da7e1a4987:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L2329-L2331",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7aadbc292065b19aaa0ec9ade9171595d53a81c258959cad724bc0714a97c76a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_6c79a894b9814774817788715384c997",
      "statement": "_llm_type (abstract property) returns a unique string identifier for the model type (e.g., 'openai', 'anthropic'). This is used for logging, tracing, and serialization. All subclasses must implement this.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L2329-L2332",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:db535b12ac0a27fd6314901aaffafb6168ea80a9f313f96f7f93ffed50846b76:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_d3b5ed8dd982413fb716ce2501fe89e1",
      "statement": "_get_ls_params() extracts LangSmith tracing parameters: ls_provider (derived from class name or overridden), ls_model_name (from kwargs['model'], self.model, or self.model_name), ls_temperature, and ls_max_tokens. Subclasses override to provide stable provider names and model identifier resolution.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L1502-L1576",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:cb5ec623ca84e8c04a65697a7e85c757abc32cf3b201a5f819234d601aca8341:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ca968af2819040e09edfeae44743ab8f",
      "statement": "_should_use_protocol_streaming() determines v2 event routing separate from v1 streaming. Routes through v2 when _V2StreamingCallbackHandler is attached and native _stream_chat_model_events, _astream_chat_model_events, or standard _stream/_astream methods are available. Uses chunks_to_events bridge to convert chunks to protocol events.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L587-L643",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:2bfd684462989559832648a165a2f3dc126ce1f8c9950d17125e7bfa8905c307:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_3bdb8e7e3d224335979da820afec7a0e",
      "statement": "_chat_model_stream_v3() returns a ChatModelStream with lazy initialization. It wraps event iteration via _iter_v2_events and uses a pump mechanism (pump_one) to lazily consume events. Rate limiting, event collection, and lifecycle callbacks are managed via closures with shared state.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L994-L1133",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:ce77e9c13ab68c17193b88c83c469b90ada207031c26fb7d00ed822f15010d46:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_78536e5312b04ae1a69c7bb45a2d0ed5",
      "statement": "generate() and agenerate() accept a list of message lists and internally batch-process them. agenerate() uses asyncio.gather with return_exceptions=True to run _agenerate_with_cache concurrently. Results are flattened and combined via _combine_llm_outputs().",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L1592-L1716",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:10713381eddb3932f6ee9ae086bc1e0e35fde2b65c37de93be4f7d5fa361ff20:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://libs/core/langchain_core/language_models/chat_models.py#L1718-L1866",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f4304f6ddc44aee6a4ec1f81b165dea18be17bc0077e61b0c0f4e0d4d857b4f7:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_b18ce93e72c247ab8ad3f21f5123766c",
      "statement": "LanguageModelInput is a union type: PromptValue | str | Sequence[MessageLikeRepresentation]. _convert_input normalizes all forms to PromptValue for downstream processing. String inputs become StringPromptValue; message sequences become ChatPromptValue.",
      "evidence": [
        {
